cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the measurement data in it, please cite the
  paper it accompanies, and this repository.
title: >-
  A finite-size crossover criterion for shadow-based moment estimation,
  with a hardware case study
abstract: >-
  Code, data, and analysis accompanying a study of when a collective
  two-copy measurement attains a lower RMSE than single-copy classical
  shadows at equal copy budget, together with a committed-in-advance
  hardware test.
authors:
  - family-names: Messerlian
    given-names: Alexander
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
  - family-names: Gu
    given-names: Ziwei
    affiliation: >-
      Harvard John A. Paulson School of Engineering and Applied Sciences
repository-code: https://github.com/alex-messerlian/shadow-moment-crossover
license: MIT
license-url: https://github.com/alex-messerlian/shadow-moment-crossover/blob/main/LICENSE
date-released: 2026-08-06
keywords:
  - classical shadows
  - randomized measurements
  - quantum state moments
  - sample complexity
  - collective measurement
